5. **Fixes are mechanical and behavior-preserving; severity decides what is asked.** After the report, run a fix pass covering only docstrings, scope-internal renames, unused imports, and dead code this project introduced. A `minor` or `nit` fix is applied unasked and named as it is applied; a `blocker` or `major` fix, and every fix that deletes code, is approved first — the whole list on the page, then one question over it (conventions §7.13), recommendation marked. Every fix is re-verified; one that fails is reverted. Never put up for approval a list the user cannot see; never "improve" adjacent code (AGENTS.md §3).
