### star-flow-status/SKILL.md
--- 1
Invocation: `star-flow-status [PLAN_NAME] [DESCRIPTION]` — with no argument, report the whole flow; with a slug / numeric prefix / filename, scope the tree and the coverage checks to that plan's subtree. Anything after `PLAN_NAME` is a description (conventions §7.12): in your own words, what this run is for. Prose resolving to no plan is description alone, not a missing target — report the whole flow, and say so in the reply's first line. A lone token that looks like a plan name and matches none is not a description: name it unmatched in that same line, since this skill never asks. A description steers what the report looks at hardest — which unknown is worth a second read, which line is worth quoting rather than counting, what the reason line addresses; it drops nothing the report owes, and never moves the next action, which the spec's priority order fixes down to the tie-break. An `involve=<level>` token is stripped before `PLAN_NAME` or the description is read (conventions §7.7); it changes nothing else here.
+++ 1
Invocation: `star-flow-status [PLAN_NAME] [DESCRIPTION]`. This run's argument is substituted here at load time — `$ARGUMENTS` — and empty backticks mean none was given. This skill runs in its own context (`context: fork`), so that substitution is the argument's only appearance: no user turn behind it to re-read, and treating a present argument as absent silently answers a question nobody asked. With no argument, report the whole flow; with a slug / numeric prefix / filename, scope the tree and the coverage checks to that plan's subtree. Anything after `PLAN_NAME` is a description (conventions §7.12): in your own words, what this run is for. Prose resolving to no plan is description alone, not a missing target — report the whole flow, and say so in the reply's first line. A lone token that looks like a plan name and matches none is not a description: name it unmatched in that same line, since this skill never asks. A description steers what the report looks at hardest — which unknown is worth a second read, which line is worth quoting rather than counting, what the reason line addresses; it drops nothing the report owes, and never moves the next action, which the spec's priority order fixes down to the tie-break. An `involve=<level>` token is stripped before `PLAN_NAME` or the description is read (conventions §7.7); it changes nothing else here.
